x86/Kconfig: enable the execmem ROX cache when STRICT_KERNEL_RWX is set

Upstream: Mike Rapoport, "x86/Kconfig: enable ROX cache in execmem when
STRICT_KERNEL_RWX is set" (lkml, 2025-09-30), resent 2026 with
Fixes: 47410d839fcd ("x86/Kconfig: only enable ROX cache in execmem when STRICT_MODULE_RWX is set")
and Acked-by Rapoport and Peter Zijlstra. Not in 6.18.62. Drop this file once the pinned kernel has it
(make fetch then fails to apply it, which is the signal).

Why this build needs it: CONFIG_MODULES=n means STRICT_MODULE_RWX does not exist, so
ARCH_HAS_EXECMEM_ROX is off and execmem_restore_rox() is an empty stub. On a host whose CPU takes the
Indirect Target Selection mitigation ("ITS: Mitigation: Aligned branch/return thunks" in the guest's
dmesg), its_pages_protect() then leaves the ITS thunk pages writable+executable, and DEBUG_WX reports
"x86/mm: Checked W+X mappings: FAILED, 6 W+X pages found" at boot. With the ROX cache the thunks end
up read-only+executable and the check passes; a one-shot "CPA detected W^X violation" warning during
alternatives patching remains (its_alloc still calls set_memory_x on the temporarily writable page,
in mainline too) and is harmless. Seen on an i9-8950HK under a RHEL 10 host kernel, 2026-11-07.

--- a/arch/x86/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/x86/Kconfig
@@ -85,7 +85,7 @@
 	select ARCH_HAS_DMA_OPS			if GART_IOMMU || XEN
 	select ARCH_HAS_EARLY_DEBUG		if KGDB
 	select ARCH_HAS_ELF_RANDOMIZE
-	select ARCH_HAS_EXECMEM_ROX		if X86_64 && STRICT_MODULE_RWX
+	select ARCH_HAS_EXECMEM_ROX		if X86_64 && (STRICT_MODULE_RWX || STRICT_KERNEL_RWX)
 	select ARCH_HAS_FAST_MULTIPLIER
 	select ARCH_HAS_FORTIFY_SOURCE
 	select ARCH_HAS_GCOV_PROFILE_ALL
